1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
From vendor noise to sourcing decisions: the Supplier Intelligence Hub.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:07,100
One sourcing portfolio can hold more than 150 vendors.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,700
Each dot is one vendor.

4
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,300
Every vendor produces signals. Some need action now.

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:17,900
The signals live in separate systems.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,500
No one person can watch all of them.

7
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,100
The Supplier Intelligence Hub collects these signals in one flow.

8
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,700
First, it reads the sources.

9
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,300
A weekly brief gives the full picture.

10
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,900
An always-on early warning watches for sudden changes.

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,500
Both send their output to one place.

12
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:43,100
Each signal gets a posture.

13
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:46,700
There are four postures. Each one tells the team what to do next.

14
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:50,300
Take Vendor X. It renews in 90 days, and the draft raises the price cap.

15
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:53,900
The posture is Increase Leverage. The team uses timing and options.

16
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,500
Now a worked example. Vendor X is fictional. All numbers are illustrative.

17
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:01,100
Vendor X costs 1 million dollars a year.

18
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:04,700
The old contract capped the yearly increase at 2 percent. That is at most 20,000 dollars.

19
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:08,300
The new draft caps it at 6 percent. That is at most 60,000 dollars.

20
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:11,900
The gap is 40,000 dollars of added exposure each year.

21
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,500
The action: ask to restore the 2 percent cap before the renewal date.

22
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:19,100
Next, how the work happens.

23
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:22,700
Everything runs in one Slack hub.

24
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:26,300
Six agents work there. Each agent has one job.

25
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:29,900
Together they turn signals into briefs, risk checks, deal support, spend views, and waste checks.

26
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,500
One more point. A strong tool should not depend on one person.

27
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:37,100
Today the hub is a personal tool.

28
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:40,700
The next step is a handoff.

29
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:44,300
A team asset has a shared data pipeline, named owners, and a written runbook.

30
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:47,900
The ask: [YOUR ASK HERE].

